fix for GHSA-2g87-pp6c-29x5 (message-tail limit, websocket reader memory stall, form-field cap, cookie caps, and domain-mask ReDoS)

The five commits below did not apply with fuzz 0 on 3.14.3. This patch keeps
only the hunks that impose the advisory limits. yarl 1.24.5 has no
query_to_pairs, so client_max_fields is a fixed cap of 1000. The cookie-parser
and cookie-jar rewrites in 6963ee0b depend on storage changes that are not in
3.14.3; the same numeric limits are applied to the existing parsers, and a new
cookie past the cap is dropped rather than evicted by LRU.

see https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/commit/3d850ee9b92573c7e913821cbcb96005beb3f4df
see https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/commit/0ae507423f681161efa77d20052b4054397c7fb6
see https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/commit/615fec3d4f088f30d2ee72cad760152e92aa1c53
see https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/commit/6963ee0befec1502b6bb7b4db6c72d044c08f4fa
see https://github.com/aio-libs/aiohttp/commit/c6ac0e44c3c573ff9616f4a6a532992538b31e43

author: Rohit Goswami (HaoZeke)

